@startuml
title Markdown Learning And Relation Persistence Flow

actor "User" as User
participant "Controller Entrypoints" as CLI
participant "SystemState" as State
participant "BSSCController" as Controller
participant "External Markdown Learning Pipeline" as Pipeline
participant "Markdown IR" as IR
participant "LLM Learning Proposals" as LLM
participant "Markdown Artifact Semantics" as Semantics
participant "Artifact Store" as Store

User -> CLI: markdown-learn --markdown-file <document>
CLI -> State: bootstrap("Learn from markdown: <file>",\nbootstrap_mode=markdown_ingestion)
CLI -> Controller: BSSCController(state, llm_policy)
CLI -> Pipeline: learn_from_markdown_document(path)

note over CLI,Pipeline
markdown-learn is a bounded document-learning pipeline.
It deconstructs markdown into reusable artifacts,
but it does not call the governed runtime loop
run() / reduce_not().
end note

Pipeline -> IR: parse_markdown_document_ir(markdown_text)
IR --> Pipeline: document IR
Pipeline -> LLM: propose_markdown_learning(root, document)
LLM --> Pipeline: knowledge artifact payloads
Pipeline -> LLM: propose_markdown_ability_learning(root, document)
LLM --> Pipeline: encounter summaries
Pipeline -> LLM: propose_markdown_functionalization(root, document, encounters)
LLM --> Pipeline: ability artifact payloads

opt direct expression fallback
  Pipeline -> Pipeline: markdown_expression_artifact_payload(...)
end

loop each accepted payload
  Pipeline -> Semantics: build_markdown_learning_artifact(...)
  opt title repair or encounter-derived answer shaping
    Semantics -> LLM: propose_markdown_title_repair(...)\nor encounter-aware shaping
    LLM --> Semantics: repaired title / semantic hints
  end
  Semantics --> Pipeline: Artifact
  Pipeline -> Store: persist_artifact(artifact)
end

Pipeline -> Pipeline: apply_markdown_batch_relations(built_artifacts)
loop each updated related artifact
  Pipeline -> Store: persist_artifact(updated_artifact)
end

Pipeline -> State: set learned artifacts,\nroot answer,\nrun outcome
CLI --> User: markdown learning report

@enduml
